        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "script",
          "title": "The letters in this word",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "પા (pā) + છા (chhā) becomes પાછા (pāchhā)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "પાછા (pāchhā, \"back, again, returning\") is from Sanskrit પશ્ચાત્ (paścāt, \"behind, afterward\") — the same \"behind/after\" root behind English post- words, distantly. It carries the sense of return: pāchhā āvvũ (\"to come back\"), pāchhā jāvũ (\"to go back\"). Add it to \"we'll meet\" and you get the warm goodbye of the next lesson."
            }
          ]
        },
